Portico bundles a curated subset of Material Design Icons as Android vector drawables
(app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_mdi_*.xml, generated by tools/gen_mdi_drawables.py).

  Material Design Icons, @mdi/svg 7.4.47, Pictogrammers (https://pictogrammers.com/library/mdi/)
  Licence: Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.txt), per the package's own LICENSE
  (LICENSE-PICTOGRAMMERS) and its package.json ("license": "Apache-2.0").

The drawables are the SVG path data of the icons named in core/src/test/resources/icons_v1.json,
converted 1:1 (24x24 viewport, one path), with no change to the shapes. The package says that a few
icons are redistributed under their own licences; the curated set is generic household symbols (doors,
locks, lights, climate, cameras, phones) and no brand logo.

One further icon, "menu" (the three-bar menu button on the Home screen's top line), is bundled the same way
as app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_menu_hamburger.xml; it is screen furniture, not a button icon, so it is
not in icons_v1.json (tools/gen_mdi_drawables.py keeps it in its CHROME list).
